sections.text:
@layer blocks push an id onto a layer stack; every rule created
while that frame is active records CurrentLayerId. Statement
layers and block layers both call GetOrAddLayer, so the layer
order is assigned once and reused. Unlayered rules keep -1, which
Data treats as stronger than every layered rule.
@keyframes sets _inKeyframes and records the
animation name. Its inner selectors (from, to,
50%) are interned like normal selectors, but each declaration
becomes a CssKeyframe rather than a matchable style rule.
Descriptor at-rules such as @font-face, @page,
@property, @counter-style,
@font-palette-values and @view-transition store their
prelude as descriptor context and their declarations as
CssDescriptor records. @page margin boxes such as
@top-center become CssMarginBox records.
@import, @charset, @namespace and
@scope are recorded as metadata. Imports are never fetched;
resolving them is the host’s job. Scope preludes are stored as interned text,
not rewritten into selectors.

